 "standard_text": "Divide whole numbers up to 48 by 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 without remainder; relate division to multiplication; solve sharing problems. (summary of the NERDC Primary 3 Mathematics curriculum)",
 "meta_desc": "Free Primary 3 maths worksheets on division: sharing equally, grouping, division facts, dividing 2-digit numbers and division word problems. 100 questions with answers.",
 "key_big": "Division is sharing equally",
 "key_sub": "12 ÷ 3 = 4 because 3 × 4 = 12.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Division means sharing equally or making equal groups.</li><li>Use the times tables: 24 ÷ 4 = 6 because 4 × 6 = 24.</li><li>A division can be checked with a multiplication.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>35 oranges shared by 5 children</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>35 ÷ 5</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 7 each</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mixing up the numbers</td><td>24 ÷ 4 is not the same as 4 ÷ 24.</td></tr><tr><td>Unequal sharing</td><td>Every group must have the same number.</td></tr><tr><td>Forgetting to check</td><td>Multiply back to check.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What is the sign for division?",
   "a": "÷."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 0 ÷ 5?",
   "a": "0."
  },
  {
   "q": "How does multiplication help?",
   "a": "If you know 6 × 7 = 42, you know 42 ÷ 6 = 7."
  }
 ],
